{"name":"Bordeaux Red","hex":"#6f2c4f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bordeaux","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Bordeaux (“fungicide; wine”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bordeaux"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red","wikidata":"Q3014419"},{"title":"Bordeaux","blocks":[{"text":"Bordeaux is a city on the river Garonne in the Gironde department, southwestern France. A port city, it is the capital of the Nouvelle-Aquitaine region, as well as the prefecture of the Gironde department. Its inhabitants are called \"Bordelais\" (masculine) or \"Bordelaises\" (feminine). The term \"Bordelais\" may also refer to the city and its surrounding region."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bordeaux_Place_de_la_Bourse_de_nuit.jpg/330px-Bordeaux_Place_de_la_Bourse_de_nuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bordeaux","wikidata":"Q1479"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":